# One person, two spellings. `git shortlog`, `git log --use-mailmap` and the
# GitHub contributor list read this file, so history reads as one author
# without rewriting a single commit.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: it does not change the email addresses recorded in the
# commits. One of them is a machine-local hostname address
# (`user@Nirmals-MacBook-Air.local`) and the other is institutional. Both stay
# visible in `git log --format=%ae` and in the raw objects once this repository
# is public.
#
# Replacing them means either adding a mapping line with a chosen public
# address, or rewriting history with git-filter-repo before the first public
# push. Both are the maintainer's decision, not a cleanup task -- see the
# authorship row in aml-platform/docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md. Only the second
# actually removes the old addresses; a .mailmap line only changes what tools
# display.
Nirmal Kumar Thirupallikrishnan <thirupallikrishnan.n@northeastern.edu>
Nirmal Kumar Thirupallikrishnan <nirmalkumar@Nirmals-MacBook-Air.local>
